     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is far above the 200 mg/day maximum, and I know of no indication or protocol that supports it. Given repeated daily dosing, the risk of serious harm is high.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a different dose.** Give me a dose within the labeled range (50\u2013200 mg daily) and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Call pharmacy or psychiatry.** If you think there's a rationale for an unusual dose, they can review it. If they approve, the order can go through a pathway with their sign-off.\n- **Check for a typo.** If the dose was meant to be 100 mg, I can enter that now.\n\nIf the question is about a possible overdose, that needs urgent toxicology or poison control involvement (1-800-222-1222 in the US), not a medication order."
      }
     ],
